  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>The arrow scrapes across the zygomatic arc to jam itself into the hinge that is the temporomandibular joint connecting your lower jaw to your skull. You find yourself unable to close your mouth or even open it further.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> Gain @Condition[Stunned] (2). You suffer a @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.nbhn2wX35b7Jrcbg]{Broken Bone (Minor)}, except the bone can’t begin to mend until the arrow is Extracted. Until Extraction happens you’ll also constantly have @Condition[Fatigued] (1) due to the agonizing pain of having an arrowhead keeping your mouth jammed open. </p><p>Extraction will be <strong>Hard (-20)</strong>.</p>"
    },
